# Sruja Architecture DSL - AI Code Generation Rules

When generating or modifying Sruja architecture DSL (.sruja files), follow these rules.

## Workflow

1. **Generate** architecture DSL based on requirements
2. **Validate** with `sruja lint <file.sruja>`
3. **Fix** any validation errors
4. **Export** to Markdown/Mermaid if needed: `sruja export markdown <file.sruja>`

## DSL Structure

1. **Define before use** – Every referenced component must be defined before use in relationships.
2. **Double quotes** – All string values: names, descriptions, technology labels.
3. **Pattern** – `[kind] "[name]" { ... }` (e.g. `container "API" { ... }`).
4. **Nesting** – Systems inside architecture, containers/datastores inside systems.
5. **Relationships** – `source -> target "label"`; one per line; descriptive labels.

## Component Kinds

```sruja
person "User" {
  description "End user of the application"
}

system "My App" {
  description "Main application system"
  
  container "Web Server" {
    technology "Node.js"
    description "HTTP server handling requests"
  }
  
  datastore "Database" {
    technology "PostgreSQL"
    description "Primary data store"
  }
}
```

## Required Fields

- **Every component**: Has a `description`.
- **Every container**: Has `technology` (e.g. "PostgreSQL", "React", "Node.js").
- **Relationships**: Use descriptive labels like "HTTPS", "gRPC", "reads from", "publishes events to".

## Multi-Repo Architecture (Microservices)

When the system spans multiple repositories, use **external systems**:

```sruja
// In user-service/architecture.sruja
system "User Service" {
  api = container "User API" {
    technology "Node.js"
    description "User management API"
  }
  
  db = datastore "User Database" {
    technology "PostgreSQL"
    description "User data storage"
  }
  
  api -> db "SQL queries"
}

// Declare external systems from other repos
order_service = external_system "Order Service" {
  description "Order processing service (separate repository)"
  metadata {
    location "github.com/org/order-service"
    tags ["external", "microservice"]
  }
}

payment_service = external_system "Payment Service" {
  description "Payment processing service (separate repository)"
  metadata {
    location "github.com/org/payment-service"
    tags ["external", "microservice"]
  }
}

// Reference external systems in relationships
user_service.api -> order_service.api "REST API"
user_service.api -> payment_service.api "gRPC"
```

## Single-Repo Architecture (Monolith)

For a single repository with all components:

```sruja
architecture "E-commerce Platform" {
  user = person "Customer" {
    description "Online shopper"
  }
  
  system "Web Application" {
    frontend = container "Web Frontend" {
      technology "React"
      description "User interface"
    }
    
    backend = container "API Server" {
      technology "Node.js"
      description "REST API server"
    }
    
    database = datastore "Database" {
      technology "PostgreSQL"
      description "Application data"
    }
    
    cache = datastore "Cache" {
      technology "Redis"
      description "Session cache"
    }
  }
  
  user -> frontend "HTTPS"
  frontend -> backend "REST API"
  backend -> database "SQL"
  backend -> cache "Redis protocol"
}
```

## Generation Prompts

### For AI Generation - Single Service

```
Generate Sruja architecture DSL for this service:
- Service name: [name]
- Technology stack: [list technologies]
- External dependencies: [list other services/databases]
- Description: [what this service does]

Rules:
- Define all components (containers, datastores) with technology labels
- Add descriptions to every component
- Use descriptive relationship labels
- Run `sruja lint` to validate after generation
```

### For AI Generation - Microservices System

```
Generate Sruja architecture DSL for a microservices system.

THIS REPOSITORY contains:
- [Service name]: [description, technologies]

EXTERNAL REPOSITORIES (declare as external systems):
- [Service name]: [description]
- [Service name]: [description]

Rules:
- Define only components in THIS repository
- Declare external services using `external system`
- Add relationships to external systems
- Add technology labels to all containers
- Run `sruja lint` to validate
```

## Best Practices

### Styling
- **2 spaces** indentation
- **Blank lines** between sections
- **Alphabetical order** for relationships when possible

### Naming
- Use **descriptive names**: "User API" not just "API"
- Use **consistent naming**: "User Service", "Order Service", not "UserService", "order-svc"
- Component IDs should be **snake_case**: `user_api`, `order_service`

### Relationships
- Be **specific**: "REST API" not "calls"
- Include **protocol**: "HTTPS", "gRPC", "AMQP"
- Include **direction**: "publishes events to", "reads from"

### Validation Rules
- **No orphans** – Every component participates in at least one relationship
- **No circular dependencies** – Between systems
- **Unique IDs** – Component IDs must be unique within the file
- **Valid references** – All relationship targets must exist

## Common Patterns

### API Gateway Pattern
```sruja
gateway = container "API Gateway" {
  technology "Kong"
  description "API gateway and rate limiter"
}

user -> gateway "HTTPS"
gateway -> user_service.api "REST"
gateway -> order_service.api "REST"
```

### Event-Driven Pattern
```sruja
message_queue = datastore "Message Queue" {
  technology "RabbitMQ"
  description "Event bus"
}

order_service.api -> message_queue "publishes OrderCreated event"
message_queue -> inventory_service.worker "consumes OrderCreated events"
```

### Database per Service
```sruja
system "User Service" {
  api = container "User API" { technology "Node.js" }
  db = datastore "User DB" { technology "PostgreSQL" }
  api -> db "SQL"
}

system "Order Service" {
  api = container "Order API" { technology "Python" }
  db = datastore "Order DB" { technology "MySQL" }
  api -> db "SQL"
}
```

## Validation

After generating, ALWAYS run:
```bash
sruja lint <file.sruja>
```

Fix any errors before committing.

## Export

Generate documentation:
```bash
sruja export markdown architecture.sruja > architecture.md
sruja export mermaid architecture.sruja > architecture.mmd
```

## Advanced: Architecture Skill

For deeper architectural guidance (patterns, trade-offs, anti-patterns):
```bash
npx skills add https://github.com/sruja-ai/sruja --skill sruja-architecture
```

